  "features": [
    "Mixed native/Node observer entries use one delivery queue, chronological takeRecords draining and correct callback receiver/owner identity.",
    "Subscription arguments and mode transitions validate before Node registry mutation; empty/unsupported multiple subscriptions disconnect and reset mode.",
    "Disconnect clears queued data and invalidates stale deliveries, including disconnect/reobserve generations in the Node registry.",
    "Ordinary local net/mark controls verify draining and same-turn coalescing to one callback in Node and Home."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Complete resource timing construction/buffering, observer supported-type breadth, entry-list branding and remaining option/error edge semantics remain open under #869.",
    "The 16-group batch precedes the final test-only coalescing assertions; that extended group was rerun separately on the same executable and passed.",
    "Pickier reports no errors and four existing style warnings in the mixed-style upstream modules.",
    "Windows measurement, Linux execution, wider startup paths, previous ICU contradiction #872, complete Bun suite, remaining native/API ownership and Release/ASAN/all-platform verification remain open under #66."
  ],
